-- SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT OR Apache-2.0
-- Accepted Bus verb registry, schema 3. Each component registers its verbs
-- here when it enters the tree (AGENTS.md §5). tools/verb_registry_gate.mix
-- checks this file against the verbs the code registers.
--
-- Two lists, one entry per line:
--   verbs:    a concrete name: {name, owner, version, status, note?, declared_by?}.
--   families: a pattern for a set of names: {pattern, owner, version, status, note?}.
--             The first segment is `<app>`, the app's own prefix, and matches
--             any one segment. A `*` segment matches exactly one later segment,
--             so "<app>.ui.*" covers "<app>.ui.tree" but not "<app>.ui.a.b".
--             A pattern never starts with `*`. Families must not overlap, and
--             every code verb must match exactly one entry (concrete or family).
--
-- The toolkit drive verbs (docs/drive.md) are one family that every egui app
-- answers under its own prefix: <app>.ui.* (tree, click, pointer, scroll, key,
-- type, menu, capture), <app>.window and <app>.window.state. The three
-- families below cover them, so an app lists only the verbs it answers itself.
--
-- owner: the component that answers the verb (its directory name).
-- declared_by: set when a different component declares the verb than the one
--   that answers it. Two shapes: a const VERBS table (libs/edit's wire.rs, which
--   editd answers), or a parse arm (libs/bus native_session/bootstrap.rs, which
--   noded answers through its SessionCommand arm). Absent means the owner declares it.
-- version: the owner's crate version at registration.
-- status: draft, accepted or retired. A retired name or pattern stays here
-- forever (AGENTS.md §3.5) and must not appear in code.
-- HELP and app.describe are protocol verbs every service answers; they are
-- not registered here.
{
  schema: 3,
  verbs: [
